   $q$Sentence 11 is a weak ending. Which sentence would be the best concluding statement to replace it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Coding builds problem solving, creativity and job skills, so our school should teach it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In conclusion, doctors and scientists use computer programs at work every day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conclusion-too-narrow"},{"text":"Learning to code is so easy that everyone can do it on the very first day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-claim"},{"text":"Coding is a good skill, but maybe kids should wait until middle school to learn it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Coding builds problem solving, creativity and job skills, so our school should teach it.$q$, $q$The best conclusion names all three reasons and repeats that the school should teach coding. The sentence about doctors and scientists starts like a conclusion, but it only repeats one detail and does not restate the opinion.$q$, 'draft', '26d9272b-30fc-5d0f-b352-27d1185d725f')
