   $q$The writer wants to join sentences 9 and 10 with a linking word. Which sentence is best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Right now, the only recycling bin is in the cafeteria until most students forget to carry their paper there.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-linking-word"},{"text":"Right now, the only recycling bin is in the cafeteria, so most students forget to carry their paper there.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Right now, the only recycling bin is in the cafeteria because most students forget to carry their paper there.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"Right now, the only recycling bin is in the cafeteria, or most students forget to carry their paper there.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-linking-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Right now, the only recycling bin is in the cafeteria, so most students forget to carry their paper there.$q$, $q$The bin being far away is the cause, and students forgetting is the result, so "so" links them correctly. "Because" flips the order and says the bin is in the cafeteria because students forget, which makes no sense.$q$, 'draft', 'f22a3a49-85eb-54e6-ae1a-95782f0642e1')
